<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="FB_MotionStageNCParams" Id="{ffafdde1-c9c9-04ad-2047-9434c7439ed8}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_MotionStageNCParams
(*
    Purpose: poll the NC parameter set of one axis and publish the selected
    subset of it to EPICS. Each refresh reads stMotionStage.Axis with
    MC_ReadParameterSet into stMotionStage.stAxisParameters, then copies the
    tunable limits out of it - max velocity, accelerations, position lag
    monitor, soft end limits, encoder scaling and offset - into
    stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed. That exposed struct is what the
    pytmc pragmas on ST_AxisParameterSetExposed publish as PLC:AxisPar, so this
    block is how the NC limits that motion commands are checked against become
    visible to the IOC.

    Usage: instantiate one per stage and call it every PLC cycle with the stage
    struct wired to stMotionStage. FB_MotionStage does exactly this, with
    bEnable hard-wired TRUE and tRefreshDelay := T#1s. This is a periodic
    refresh, not a command: there is nothing to acknowledge, reset or wait for.
    Reads are paced so the NC is not polled every scan - the request latch
    bExecute is set by timer.Q tRefreshDelay after the previous read finished
    and dropped on Done or Error - while the copy into
    stAxisParametersExposed runs every scan from the last completed read, so
    EPICS always shows the most recent successful values. Nothing here detects
    a missing read: if the refresh stops, the published parameters simply stay
    at their last values. stMotionStage.bAxisParamsInit is latched TRUE by the
    first completed read and never cleared by this block; it is the project's
    "axis parameters have been read at least once" flag, which other blocks use
    to tell "not read yet" from "read, and the values happen to be zero".

    Objectives:
    - Keep the NC parameters current in the PLC without every caller writing
      its own polling logic or issuing a parameter read every single cycle.
    - Publish the configured limits in engineering units so operators and the
      IOC can see what the motion commands are actually limited to.
    - Keep a failed read observable through bError instead of letting stale
      parameters look current.

    Author: Zachary Lentz <zlentz@slac.stanford.edu>
    History: 2020-07-08  Zachary Lentz    created with the PMPS implementation
                                          baseline
             2020-07-14  Zachary Lentz    midnight hour bugfixes
             2023-03-15  Zachary Lentz    DUT_MotionStage renamed ST_MotionStage
                                          (find/replace)
             2023-05-18  Zachary Lentz    project version pinned outside of the
                                          individual files
             2024-04-04  Nicholas Lentz   added ST_AxisParameterSetExposed and the
                                          copy of the selected parameters
             2024-04-08  Nicholas Lentz   exposed encoder scaling and offset
             2026-11-27  Scirix Agent     added purpose/usage/objectives/history and
                                          declaration comments, no logic changed
                                          (audit finding #340, task #190)
*)
VAR_IN_OUT
    // The motor whose parameters are read and published: Axis is the NC axis
    // handed to MC_ReadParameterSet, stAxisParameters receives that function
    // block's ST_AxisParameterSet output (Tc2_MC2 struct, each field in its own
    // NC unit - see the fields listed in the body), stAxisParametersExposed is
    // the subset copied out for EPICS, and bAxisParamsInit is latched TRUE here
    // after the first completed read.
    stMotionStage: ST_MotionStage;
END_VAR
VAR_INPUT
    // Level enable for the refresh: while FALSE, Execute on mcReadParams is
    // held FALSE, so no new parameter read is started and the published values
    // stay at their last read. Normal operation keeps this TRUE for the whole
    // life of the PLC, as FB_MotionStage does.
    bEnable: BOOL;
    // Off-time between parameter reads, as a TIME. TwinCAT TIME has 1 ms
    // resolution, so this is a duration in ms (T#1s = 1000 ms) - not a cycle
    // count and not an engineering-unit quantity. It is counted from the end of
    // the previous read, so the real refresh period is tRefreshDelay plus the
    // time the NC takes to answer. This is a polling interval only: it is not a
    // timeout, and nothing here faults or gives up if a read never completes.
    tRefreshDelay: TIME;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    // Pass-through of MC_ReadParameterSet.Error for the most recent read
    // request. TRUE means that read came back as failed - typically an invalid
    // axis reference, an NC that is not configured, or an unknown parameter -
    // and FALSE means it did not. This block does not latch it: bError is
    // re-assigned on every call, so it follows the function block's own reset
    // behaviour and drops as soon as that clears it, at the latest when the next
    // refresh is issued. It does not raise stMotionStage.bError and is not
    // counted anywhere, so a caller that needs a latched read fault has to latch
    // it itself.
    bError: BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR
    // TwinCAT NC function block that reads one parameter set from one axis.
    // Parameter is stMotionStage.stAxisParameters (the destination struct),
    // Axis is stMotionStage.Axis, Execute is the request latch bExecute below,
    // Error goes to this block's bError, and ErrorID is inspected for
    // nLatchErrId. Busy/Done/Error are the handshake that clears bExecute.
    mcReadParams: MC_ReadParameterSet;
    // Pacing timer for the refresh (TON, PT := tRefreshDelay in ms): it runs
    // while bEnable is TRUE and no read is pending, and its Q sets the request
    // latch. Because its IN is bEnable AND NOT bExecute, it is held reset for
    // the whole duration of a read, so the delay it measures is the off-time
    // after a read completes rather than the total period.
    timer: TON;
    // Request latch for mcReadParams.Execute. Initialised TRUE so that the first
    // parameter read is issued on the very first scan instead of one
    // tRefreshDelay later. Set again by timer.Q, reset when the read reports
    // Done or Error, and inverted into the timer's IN to hold the timer off
    // while a read is in flight.
    bExecute: BOOL := TRUE;
    // Placeholder for the NC error id of a failed parameter read: a TwinCAT NC
    // error code (UDINT, dimensionless - not an engineering value or a count).
    // Only written as 0 today, whenever mcReadParams.ErrorID is non-zero; no
    // code ever stores the id itself, so it always reads 0 and carries no
    // information. Kept as the intended home for a latched read error id.
    nLatchErrId: UDINT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[timer(
    IN:=bEnable AND NOT bExecute,
    PT:=tRefreshDelay);
bExecute S= timer.Q;
mcReadParams(
    Parameter:=stMotionStage.stAxisParameters,
    Axis:=stMotionStage.Axis,
    Execute:=bEnable AND bExecute,
    Error=>bError);

// Copy axis parameters that we want to expose to the EPICS layer.
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.bCtrlEnablePosDiffControl     := stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.bCtrlEnablePosDiffControl;
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.bEncEnableSoftEndMaxControl   := stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.bEncEnableSoftEndMaxControl;
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.bEncEnableSoftEndMinControl   := stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.bEncEnableSoftEndMinControl;
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.fAccelerationMax              := stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.fAccelerationMax;
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.fCtrlPosDiffMax               := stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.fCtrlPosDiffMax;
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.fCtrlPosDiffMaxTime           := stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.fCtrlPosDiffMaxTime;
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.fDecelerationMax              := stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.fDecelerationMax;
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.fEncSoftEndMax                := stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.fEncSoftEndMax;
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.fEncSoftEndMin                := stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.fEncSoftEndMin;
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.fVeloMaximum                  := stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.fVeloMaximum;
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.fEncOffset               		:= stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.fEncOffset;
stMotionStage.stAxisParametersExposed.fEncScaleFactorInternal       := stMotionStage.stAxisParameters.fEncScaleFactorInternal;

IF mcReadParams.ErrorID <> 0 THEN
    nLatchErrId := 0;
END_IF
bExecute R= mcReadParams.Done OR mcReadParams.Error;
stMotionStage.bAxisParamsInit S= mcReadParams.Done;]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>